          "afterLines": [
            "- **I2:** callback/sync/promises readFile inspect actual write-capable flags before internal binding can open a protected path. The checked flag is nonwritable and nonconfigurable only on a private options copy, so native option processing cannot replace it. The caller's original options object stays unchanged, and other option descriptors are preserved. Ordinary data flags still pass to the original API with its actual native result/exception; numeric fds/native FileHandle reads do not open again. This is a static source correction, with no getter example or candidate execution. Node26 disposable mkdir entry points check the prefix and actual returned path; wrapper descriptors/prototype/path and real remove/dispose return/error behavior remain, but each disposer rechecks its captured actual path boundary. Default ReadStream is **not** listed as a proven bypass; its actual open goes through the existing open wrapper.\n"
